15 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237922 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237922 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237922 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- $B={A}^{-1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237922 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98689422-75b7-52ec-a8b8-4a4a4c165a7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237922 #edb/ref 1074 "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $B={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -5 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250827 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250827 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250827 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "203d12f3-8c3a-5557-837d-97614900aecd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251017 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #ed